 lines=intro+['','Numerical histories are H-MULTI except the interception C02 H-CURRENT leader; the carry selector chooses among H-MULTI output recipes using earlier current-season score memory. Receptions has the preserved D2/C02 static tie. Chart-PPR ranks only the supported qualified labels; unresolved rare-component completeness prevents an unrestricted exact-chart or website-fantasy parity claim. Native units differ and must not be ranked against each other. Every winner above is best among the verified comparable tested procedures on its stated product/panel.','','A challenger may advance provisionally through the retained owner under the existing authorized policy without a new blanket wait or an invented universal website-relative-win prerequisite. This does not establish a verified website improvement or scientific qualification. Own source/model recovery, identity/target/functional, inference, consumer, fallback, freshness, rollback and owner admission remain mandatory. [Exact current/prepared policy and actual capture states](PROVISIONAL_POLICY_AND_CAPTURE_STATUS.json).','','## B. Current-season method comparisons','','The first table in each category is the complete fixed W1–7 numerical recipe grid, including unrun exact current cells. The second is the registered two-week rolling offered-threshold reconstruction: Over/Under/Combined counts use selected side, not realized side. Point source, distribution law and chronological selector are separate identities. Price/EV/ROI/CLV remain unavailable. Full record IDs, code/config hashes, source tiers and cutoffs are in [finite roster](roster/finite-v2/README.md), [bindings](REPORT_BINDINGS.json) and permanent canonical scores.','']
